<p>Pakistan is stepping more openly into efforts to help ease the war involving the United States, Israel and Iran, with officials in Islamabad signaling that they are ready to facilitate or host talks if Washington and Tehran agree. The idea has drawn attention in Washington, where Congressman Tom Suozzi described Pakistan as an important neutral party, while Pakistan&#x27;s ambassador to the United States said the country’s ties with the US, Iran and Gulf states give it a chance to help. The opening is still tentative. Pakistan’s Foreign Office urged the media and the public not to speculate before any official announcement, even as Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif formally offered Islamabad as a venue for meaningful and conclusive talks. Reporting from several outlets suggests Pakistan has been in touch with a wide range of capitals as part of that effort, though analysts note that Islamabad’s defense relationship with Saudi Arabia could complicate its claim to neutrality if the regional war widens further.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/BBgRnhEXrYRSV3VV7PI6IGgaqkOts8y4iK_tt8By5Jewtphigii9mtuoMGjyUzIGwQVAJUtrCJeWdA0FFnNq4oenQ09qmTKX7cb0GvKWQqcLoWCcw1j2VrB6qRYxADjOFJjkmqvnh85BepPzoxAk3qmIMcMfJ4YNpiTTxjx1TfoioYCxUR_p3WAkrERIJbL93edmkxYOrzPQ0kbBa2I' alt='Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif of Pakistan.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Regional outreach: Pakistan has called Washington, Tehran, Riyadh, Abu Dhabi, Cairo, Istanbul and Brussels as it tries to keep diplomatic channels open across rival camps.</li><li>Channel logic: Dawn reported that Washington has relied on regional actors to keep communication channels with Iran open, helping explain why Pakistan’s offer has gained traction.</li><li>Indirect contacts: Foreign Minister Ishaq Dar confirmed that Iran and the United States are holding indirect negotiations, a sign that mediation efforts have moved beyond public signaling.</li><li>Venue speculation: Dawn cited Reuters, Axios and The Guardian as saying Islamabad was being considered as a possible site for talks if mediation progressed smoothly.</li></ul><blockquote>We would only be too honored if we are trusted by both sides to be a facilitator. - Rizwan Sheikh</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pakistan government: Since the conflict began, Pakistan’s civilian and military leadership have engaged leaders in regional and friendly countries while pressing for de-escalation. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1985566/is-pakistan-hosting-us-iran-talks-heres-what-we-know-so-far'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Pakistan Foreign Office: The Foreign Office said Pakistan’s position is in line with its longstanding policy of resolving the Middle East/Persian Gulf conflict through dialogue and diplomacy. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1985566/is-pakistan-hosting-us-iran-talks-heres-what-we-know-so-far'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>US Congressional Pakistan Caucus: Suozzi argued that Pakistan’s demographic scale — including its fifth-largest population and its potential to become the largest Muslim-majority nation — could give it greater diplomatic weight over time. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1985823/very-important-neutral-party-pakistan-can-play-greater-diplomatic-role-says-us-lawmaker'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>NDTV analysis: NDTV argued that any spillover of the war into Saudi Arabia would test Pakistan’s claim to neutrality because of its defense commitments to Riyadh. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-news-pakistans-peace-broker-role-in-iran-us-war-has-a-saudi-problem-11272541#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1985823/very-important-neutral-party-pakistan-can-play-greater-diplomatic-role-says-us-lawmaker'>‘Very important neutral party’: Pakistan can play greater diplomatic role, says US lawmaker</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-news-pakistans-peace-broker-role-in-iran-us-war-has-a-saudi-problem-11272541#publisher=newsstand'>Pakistan&#x27;s Peace Broker Role In Iran-US War Has A Saudi Problem</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/26/world/asia/pakistan-iran-united-states-talks.html'>Pakistan, Playing Mediator Between U.S. and Iran, Is Calling Several Countries</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://thepakistanconnect.com/pakistan-acting-as-mediator-between-us-iran/'>Pakistani foreign minister Ishaq Dar confirms that indirect negotiations between Iran and the U.S. are taking place.</a> - thepakistanconnect.com</li></ul>